addrmap hi3516dv300 {
    name = "hi3516dv300 registers";
    desc = "
## Status

Register map of the Hi3516D V300 (Hi3516C V500 family: dual Cortex-A7, NNIE neural network engine, 4K encode, MIPI RX/TX, HDMI, VDP).
Everything below is taken from the HiSilicon Hi3516D V300 Professional Smart IP Camera SoC data sheet (Issue 01, 2019-09-12): the address map (table 1-2), the interrupt table (table 3-6) and the register tables of chapters 3 to 13.
The register blocks were extracted programmatically from the data sheet text (names, offsets, bit ranges, access, reset values, short descriptions) and are labelled PROVEN (data sheet table).
Blocks whose IP is the same as on the other Hi3516 V300 family chips reuse the shared blocks in rdl/common (or the Hi3516A V300 chip-local CRG); their offsets and names were compared one by one with the data sheet tables of this chip (see docs/rdl-campaign/hi3516dv300-datasheet.md of the workspace for the per-block result). Bit-range differences between a data sheet table and a shared block are mostly reserved bits the data sheet omits.
Not modelled because the data sheet gives no register tables: SCD, VPSS, VIPROC, TDE, JPGE, JPGD, IVE, VGS, DDRT, GZIP, KLAD, GDC, NNIE, VEDU/VENC, HDMI, ISP (the MPP registers are not published in this data sheet); I/O control (pin mux) and the two-channel PWM groups are summarized only in the pin chapter, not as register tables.
Registers whose offset contains a variable (VICAP PT_N/CH_N, MIPI RX N/M, DDRC ports/regions/groups, TZASC sec_regions, QoS buffer chans) are modelled as arrays with the value ranges of the data sheet variable tables (checked 2026-11-15). The Hi3516C V500 (brief data sheet only, no register map) is a sibling part with the same CPU subsystem and peripheral list; its register map is assumed, not verified, to equal this one.
Nothing was verified on hardware (no Hi3516D V300 board on the bench).

## Addresses

| Start Address | End Address | Description | Documented Here |
|---------------|-------------|-------------|-----------------|
| 0x00000000 | 0x03FFFFFF | During remapping: BOOTROM | &#10060; |
| 0x04000000 | 0x0400FFFF | BOOTROM address space | &#10060; |
| 0x04010000 | 0x04019FFF | Address space of the on-chip RAM | &#10060; |
| 0x0401B000 | 0x0FFFFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x10000000 | 0x1000FFFF | FMC register | &#9989; FMC (reused common block) |
| 0x10010000 | 0x1001FFFF | ETH register | &#9989; ETH (reused common block) |
| 0x10020000 | 0x1002FFFF | SDIO1 register | &#9989; SDIO1 (reused common block) |
| 0x10030000 | 0x1003FFFF | SCD register | &#10060; |
| 0x10040000 | 0x1005FFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x10060000 | 0x1006FFFF | DMAC register | &#9989; DMAC (reused common block) |
| 0x10070000 | 0x1007FFFF | KLAD register | &#10060; |
| 0x10080000 | 0x1008FFFF | RSA0 register | &#9989; RSA0 (reused common block) |
| 0x10090000 | 0x1009FFFF | TRNG register | &#9989; TRNG (reused common block) |
| 0x100A0000 | 0x100AFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x100B0000 | 0x100BFFFF | OTP_USER register | &#9989; OTP_USER (reused common block) |
| 0x100C0000 | 0x100CFFFF | SPACC register | &#9989; SPACC (reused common block) |
| 0x100D0000 | 0x100DFFFF | RSA1 register | &#9989; RSA1 (reused common block) |
| 0x100E0000 | 0x100EFFFF | USB control register | &#9989; USB (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x100F0000 | 0x100FFFFF | SDIO0 register | &#9989; SDIO0 (reused common block) |
| 0x10100000 | 0x1010FFFF | eMMC register | &#9989; EMMC (reused common block) |
| 0x10110000 | 0x1011FFFF | USB PHY register | &#9989; USB2_PHY (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x10120000 | 0x10FEFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x10FF0000 | 0x10FFFFFF | I/O control register | &#10060; |
| 0x11000000 | 0x1103FFFF | VIPROC register | &#10060; |
| 0x11040000 | 0x1104FFFF | VPSS register | &#10060; |
| 0x11050000 | 0x110FFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x11100000 | 0x1110FFFF | NNIE register | &#10060; |
| 0x11110000 | 0x1111FFFF | GDC register | &#10060; |
| 0x11120000 | 0x111EFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x111F0000 | 0x111FFFFF | I/O control register | &#10060; |
| 0x11200000 | 0x1120FFFF | GZIP register | &#10060; |
| 0x11210000 | 0x1121FFFF | TDE register | &#10060; |
| 0x11220000 | 0x1122FFFF | JPGE register | &#10060; |
| 0x11230000 | 0x1123FFFF | IVE register | &#10060; |
| 0x11240000 | 0x1124FFFF | VGS register | &#10060; |
| 0x11250000 | 0x1125FFFF | DDRT register | &#10060; |
| 0x11260000 | 0x1126FFFF | JPGD register | &#10060; |
| 0x11270000 | 0x1127FFFF | MIPI TX register | &#9989; MIPI_TX (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x11280000 | 0x112EFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x112F0000 | 0x112FFFFF | I/O control register | &#10060; |
| 0x11300000 | 0x1139FFFF | VICAP register | &#9989; VICAP (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x113A0000 | 0x113AFFFF | MIPI RX register | &#9989; MIPI_RX (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x113B0000 | 0x113BFFFF | Audio input audio output (AIAO) | &#9989; AIAO (reused common block) |
| 0x113C0000 | 0x113CFFFF | Audio codec register | &#9989; ACODEC (generated from the data sheet) |
| 0x113D0000 | 0x113FFFFF | Reserved | &#10060; |
| 0x11400000 | 0x1140FFFF | HDMI PHY register | &#10060; |
